{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1773084773,"nonce":"DHL8sQEvxZVS4yz2IcxUWoaY2CM=","message":"Additional context from design discussion:\n\n## Live animation intent (more specific than \"animate node state changes\")\n\nThe vision for session/agent nodes is that they visually *move* — attaching to issue nodes when work starts, detaching when work ends, pulsing or glowing while active. This is not just a status color change but a spatial/animated relationship: an agent node drifts toward and connects to an issue node as it begins work, then dissolves the edge or floats away on completion. Auth requests similarly appear as a node that connects to a branch and then to an issue, and disappears on resolution. The graph should feel alive during an active work session.\n\n## Related: back/forward navigation history (#4523363)\n\nIssue 4523363 (back/forward navigation history for cross-tab deep links) is directly relevant to the GraphView. The graph is likely to be a high-traffic navigation hub — clicking nodes to jump between issues, sessions, auth requests. Without back/forward history, navigating back to the graph after following a link requires re-opening it manually. The GraphView implementation should be designed with the expectation that 4523363 will be implemented, and ideally the two efforts coordinate on how graph node clicks integrate with navigation history.\n\n## Future: shared graph infrastructure module\n\nLong-term consideration: if HumbleB gains more specialized visual representation (see HumbleB issue cf51a72), there may be value in extracting the low-level graph rendering primitives into a shared module (e.g. `@mll/graph-canvas` npm package) that both Mandible and HumbleB depend on. This would avoid duplicating Sigma/D3 setup, typed node/edge wire format, and basic layout configuration. Not a near-term requirement — both apps can develop their graph views independently — but worth designing with this in mind so the extraction path is not blocked.","files":null}]}